istered, interactionally controlled, and sensitive to recipient design. Several general consequences of the model are explicated, and contrasts are sketched with turn-taking organizations for other speech-exchange systems.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2307/412243", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2006, 5, 11]], "date-time": "2006-05-11T10:33:41Z", "timestamp": 1147343621000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 9222, "title": ["A simplest systematics for the organization of turn-taking for conversation"], "author": [{"given": "Harvey", "family": "Sacks", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Emanuel A.", "family": "Schegloff", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Gail", "family": "Jefferson", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "container-title": ["Language"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[1974, 12]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[1974, 12]]}}, {"DOI": "10.3115/v1/d14-1181", "type": "proceedings-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2015, 6, 17]], "date-time": "2015-06-17T03:07:54Z", "timestamp": 1434510474000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 9170, "title": ["Convolutional Neural Networks for Sentence Classification"], "author": [{"given": "Yoon", "family": "Kim", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "container-title": ["Proceedings of the 2014 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2014]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2014]]}}, {"DOI": "10.1017/cbo9780511813085", "type": "monograph", "created": {"date-parts": [[2018, 6, 1]], "date-time": "2018-06-01T05:42:31Z", "timestamp": 1527831751000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 9078, "title": ["Politeness"], "author": [{"given": "Penelope", "family": "Brown", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []